course: dictionary
lesson: 7545
title: Preen: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The best way to find the right one is to read the words around it. «Birds preen to keep their feathers clean, tidy and waterproof.» The subject is a bird, so preen means to clean and tidy its feathers with its beak.
explain: The same word can describe a person too. When someone preens in front of the mirror, they spend a long time making themselves look nice. Writers often use this meaning when they are joking or disapproving, so the word sounds a little vain.
explain: You can also preen yourself on something, which means to feel or show pride in yourself. Ask yourself who or what is doing the preening. A bird, a person, or someone feeling proud? Then choose the meaning that fits best.
fact: When a bird preens, it cleans and tidies its feathers with its beak.
fact: «Preen» can also mean to spend a lot of time making yourself look nice, often in a joking or disapproving way.
fact: «Preen yourself on something» means to feel or show pride in yourself.
fact: «Ducks spread oil from a gland near the tail over their feathers when they preen, so water runs off.» That is why they preen so much.
fact: Preening keeps feathers good for flying, because it helps birds zip their feathers back together.
exercise: «Birds preen to keep their feathers clean, tidy and waterproof.» What does preen mean here? | *To clean and tidy feathers with the beak | To fly very high over the trees | To sing loudly at dawn
exercise: Ellie says the boy would preen in front of the mirror all morning. What does preen mean? | *To spend a lot of time making yourself look nice | To dive under water | To count your coins
exercise: «She was preening herself on winning the race.» What does preening herself show? | Hunger for lunch | *Pride in herself | Tiredness after running
test: «Ducks spread oil from a gland near the tail over their feathers when they preen.» Which word best describes what the duck is doing to its feathers? | Painting them | *Cleaning and tidying them | Pulling them out
test: Dad says, «Stop preening and get in the car!» What does he mean? | Stop flying around | Stop singing loudly | *Stop spending so long making yourself look nice
exam: Which sentence uses preen to mean a bird cleaning its feathers? | Ella will preen before the show | *The swan stopped to preen its feathers on the lake | Ben will preen for the photo
